  "note": "The same 500 m2 pad-and-vent greenhouse, same baby-leaf lettuce band, same equipment and the same manual prices, repeated at the site fields of the five bundled climates: Tulsa, Phoenix, Miami, Denver and Seattle. The tool compares sites by running one unchanged facility at each of them, and this file is only the facility half of that comparison: each scenario carries the latitude, longitude, time zone and ZIP of its site, and you still select the matching bundled weather year for that site in the interface before running it. Latitude, longitude and time zone are what drive the solar geometry and the local day, so a scenario run against another site record reports that other record under this site name. Prices are left on manual and identical everywhere on purpose, so any cost difference you see is climate and dispatch, not tariff.",
